  "transcriptContext": "Knox’s original example on our six-handed table: you hold A♠ 5♠ in the big blind with blinds of 5 and 10 and 1,000 in every stack. The hand is dealt as he says it changes the hand. Rae, Ned and Kit fold, and as he names the late open, the button tag lights and Ivy raises to 25 from the button, her chips flying to the pot; Sol folds from the small blind, and it is your turn with 15 to call. Your two cards light as he names ace-five suited, the ace rings as he says it blocks ace-king and ace-queen, and both spades lift as he names the nut flush. Beside the table, value and pressure are named only as he says them, then the leak. The seat, the blinds, the stacks and the size of the open are given for the exercise; Knox does not speak them. The film shows no 3-bet, recommends no action, and turns over no opponent card. The original voice and speaking animation play continuously at their original speed.",
